highest F1-score. Model 5 achieved the fewest wrong labels
(18), while Model 1 exhibited the fewest false positives (25),
false negatives (21), and wrong cases (52). For partial-arch
IOSs, Model 5 achieved the best overall performance across
all metrics. Although Model 3 had the fewest false positives
(37), Model 5 had the fewest false negatives (23), wrong labels
(56), and wrong cases (64). Based on these results, Model 5
was selected as the best ﬁnal model for this study.
